Imports:
  - Types:
      - NestContainer
      - Injector
      - InstanceWrapper
    From: packages/core/injector
  - Types:
      - AbstractHttpAdapter
    From: packages/core/adapters
  - Types:
      - GuardsConsumer
      - GuardsContextCreator
    From: packages/core/guards
  - Types:
      - PipesConsumer
      - PipesContextCreator
    From: packages/core/pipes
  - Types:
      - InterceptorsConsumer
      - InterceptorsContextCreator
    From: packages/core/interceptors
  - Types:
      - NotFoundException
      - ForbiddenException
    From: packages/common/exceptions

Annotations: |
  This cell is the HTTP request-execution orchestrator: for every controller method
  discovered on every module in `NestContainer`, it builds one composed handler that
  runs guards, then pipes, then interceptors (wrapping the handler call itself), and
  registers that composed handler on the `AbstractHttpAdapter` in use. It is the root
  of the request-handling spine — the point where the DI container, the platform
  adapter, and all three extension mechanisms meet.

---

"RoutesResolver(container: NestContainer, applicationConfig: any, injector: Injector, graphInspector: any)":
  location: routes-resolver.ts
  annotations: |
    Top-level entry point for route registration: walks every module in `container`
    and registers each of its controllers' routes on the active HTTP adapter.

    `container`: `NestContainer` from Imports, source of the module graph
    `injector`: `Injector` from Imports, passed down to per-route registration
  methods:
    "resolve(applicationRef: any, globalPrefix: string, options: Object<string, any>)": |
      For every module in the container this resolver was constructed with,
      register that module's controllers' routes on `applicationRef` under
      `globalPrefix`.
    "registerRouters(routes: Object<string, InstanceWrapper>, moduleName: string, globalPrefix: string, modulePath: string, applicationRef: any, options: Object<string, any>)": |
      For each controller `InstanceWrapper` in `routes`, resolve its host/version
      metadata and its controller-level path(s), then delegate per-path route
      exploration to `RouterExplorer`.
    "registerNotFoundHandler()": |
      Register a fallback handler on the active `AbstractHttpAdapter` from Imports
      that throws `NotFoundException` from Imports for any request that reached it
      unmatched.
    "registerExceptionHandler()": |
      Register the active `AbstractHttpAdapter`'s central error handler, translating
      any error that reaches it through the adapter's own exception-mapping method
      before re-throwing it into the exception-filter pipeline.

"RouterExplorer(metadataScanner: any, container: NestContainer, injector: Injector, routerProxy: any, exceptionsFilter: any, config: any, routePathFactory: any, graphInspector: any)":
  location: router-explorer.ts
  annotations: |
    Scans one controller instance for its @Get()/@Post()/... handler methods and,
    for each one, builds a `RouterExecutionContext`-produced request handler and
    registers it on the HTTP adapter at the resolved path.

    On construction, assembles one shared `RouterExecutionContext` wired to fresh
    `PipesContextCreator`/`PipesConsumer`, `GuardsContextCreator`/`GuardsConsumer`,
    and `InterceptorsContextCreator`/`InterceptorsConsumer` pairs from Imports.
  methods:
    "explore(instanceWrapper: InstanceWrapper, moduleKey: string, httpAdapterRef: any, host: string | Array<string>, routePathMetadata: Object<string, any>, options: Object<string, any>)": |
      Scan the controller instance held by `instanceWrapper` for handler methods and
      register each discovered route on `httpAdapterRef`.
    "extractRouterPath(metatype: Object<string, any>) -> paths: Array<string>": |
      Read the controller-level path metadata off `metatype`; throws if a controller
      class has no @Controller() path metadata at all.

"RouterExecutionContext(paramsFactory: any, pipesContextCreator: PipesContextCreator, pipesConsumer: PipesConsumer, guardsContextCreator: GuardsContextCreator, guardsConsumer: GuardsConsumer, interceptorsContextCreator: InterceptorsContextCreator, interceptorsConsumer: InterceptorsConsumer, applicationRef: any)":
  location: router-execution-context.ts
  annotations: |
    Builds the actual per-route request handler function bound to the HTTP adapter:
    the composition point where guards, pipes and interceptors (all from Imports)
    are combined around one controller method.
  methods:
    "create(instance: any, callback: Object<string, any>, methodName: string, moduleKey: string, requestMethod: string, contextId: Object<string, any>, inquirerId: string) -> handler: Object<string, any>": |
      `instance`: the controller instance owning `callback`
      `callback`: the handler method being wired up
      `moduleKey`: the module the controller belongs to, used to resolve
      module-scoped guards/pipes/interceptors

      Algorithm:
      1. Resolve this handler's argument metadata, pipes (`PipesContextCreator`),
         guards (`GuardsContextCreator`), and interceptors
         (`InterceptorsContextCreator`) for `moduleKey`
      2. Build a request handler that: runs the resolved guards via `GuardsConsumer`,
         raising `ForbiddenException` from Imports when they deny the request;
         sets the configured response status and headers; then invokes
         InterceptorsConsumer.intercept, passing a callback that first applies the
         resolved pipes to the handler's arguments (`PipesConsumer`) and then calls
         the real `callback`
      3. Return the composed handler, ready to be registered on the HTTP adapter for
         this route

